<p>European Union regulators have opened a formal investigation into fast-fashion e-commerce platform Shein. They’re looking at whether the company is meeting its obligations under the bloc’s Digital Services Act (DSA), including rules on illegal products, user protection, and concerns about allegedly “addictive” design features. Several reports say the probe was prompted in part by sexually inappropriate items appearing on the site, including listings described as “childlike” sex dolls, raising questions about the platform’s safeguards. Shein said it removed the products right away and has banned sex dolls from its site worldwide.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/faaxPJbT7LKyxHYk-zVdUomKkHEOaAH9-y_bAdz7d52SA7mV3d2CTaUt-itlkOOii4DAczdU6Rx1OzxkxCW-5zgHG2y0AOtQ6htZwB77w1pX8CumsdVEzOo7K3zml4dKt3GhjbD_SwG_2e91XcoYRrk1z49M0rZ8QxS9pZB82_t3B9etjXP4DQY8-0D97vVG9KDu7aoamlEC2c8oPNEA' alt='A Shein-related photo from France as EU regulators scrutinize the platform.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Earlier scrutiny in France: Semafor reports that French authorities tried to suspend Shein in November, shortly after it opened its first physical store in Paris, amid accusations the site was selling “childlike” sex dolls.</li><li>Wider enforcement moment: The Shein probe lands as Europe steps up parallel investigations into major online services — including cases in Spain involving Meta, X and TikTok, plus a separate Ireland case involving X’s chatbot, according to Semafor.</li><li>Competitive backdrop: Semafor notes Shein and other Chinese e-commerce companies have grown quickly across Europe in recent years, drawing closer regulatory attention.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>European Union regulators: EU authorities say they’re examining whether Shein is complying with the DSA, including requirements tied to illegal products, user protection, and allegedly addictive design features. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/shein-under-investigation-in-eu-over-illegal-products-and-addictive-online-design-features'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li><li>Shein: Shein said it removed the flagged products and has banned sex dolls from its site globally. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/eu-investigates-shein-over-sale-of-childlike-sex-dolls'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Semafor reporting: Semafor links the EU investigation to growing scrutiny of Shein’s European footprint, including French authorities’ earlier attempt to suspend the company in November after it opened its first physical store in Paris. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/17/2026/eu-investigates-shein-shopping-sites-addictive-design'>Semafor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/shein-under-investigation-in-eu-over-illegal-products-and-addictive-online-design-features'>Shein under investigation in EU over illegal products and addictive online design features</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/shein-faces-eu-investigation-over-products-design-features/a-76011964'>Shein faces EU investigation over products, design features</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cr7321n1n0eo'>Shein under EU investigation over childlike sex dolls</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/eu-investigates-shein-over-sale-of-childlike-sex-dolls'>EU investigates Shein over sale of childlike sex dolls</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/17/2026/eu-investigates-shein-shopping-sites-addictive-design'>EU investigates Shein over shopping site&#x27;s ‘addictive design’</a> - semafor.com</li></ul>